      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{61734d8acc7413744089269c|full_name} Turns out shortly after posting this, some creator friends of mines informed me that we no longer really need to make a separate project for the quest version of our worlds.\n\nThough some creator friends of mines don't use stuff like EasyQuestSwitch. Reason unknown. My only guess is perhaps it's just outdated information on what the best practices are???\n\nI only found out recently we can use shaders other than the VRChat ones in worlds too.\n\nI also didn't know about the network ID thing or how it handles between versions of the world or if that's important.\n\nMy question then is if the multi-build uploading would respect a tool like EasyQuestSwitch?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
